	(text "FujiNet for the Nintendo Entertainment System - Rev1 (two RP2354Bs, no SRAM)\n\nRP-A (U1) sits on the CPU side of the 5V cart bus through its 5V-tolerant pads: CPU A0-A14, D0-D7, M2, R/W,\n/ROMSEL in, /IRQ out, PPU A12 in (MMC3 IRQ).  It serves PRG from RAM (images up to 384K) or from its in-package\nflash through QMI address translation (512K), plus $5000-$7FFF, the loader and the vectors, and runs the mappers.\nRP-B (U2) sits on the PPU side: PPU A0-A13, D0-D7, /RD, /WR in; CIRAM A10 and /CE out.  It serves CHR, CHR-RAM\nand four-screen nametables from RAM and has no firmware of its own: RP-A loads it over SWD (GP44-46) at every\nboot.  RP-A forwards every mapper write to RP-B over an 8-bit link (LD0-7, LCLK, LFRM, LACK back).\nEach RP's whole supply (IOVDD, core regulator input) runs from its own AP2112K off +5V (+3V3_RP, +3V3_RPB),\nso the pads are powered whenever the console bus is.  PWR_OK = 0.6 x CONS_5V (2.2k / 3.3k) into both RPs:\nthe data lines and CIRAM stay off the bus until the console is on; RP-B also reads it on its ADC.\nESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 runs FujiNet (fujiversal-nes) and is the USB host of RP-A (CDC, VID 0xCafe);\nS3 IO4/IO5 force RP-A RUN/QSPI_SS so the S3 can re-flash RP-A over PICOBOOT.\nUSB-C: power + CP2102N UART bridge for flashing the S3.  microSD on S3 SPI.  CIClone (ATtiny13A) on the\nCIC fingers, DNP until its firmware exists.\nEdge: 72 pins, 2.50 mm pitch, 1-36 on the label side, pin 1 at the RIGHT seen from the label side with the\nfingers down (nesdev Cartridge connector; NES-EWROM-01 geometry).  EXP, SYSTEM CLK and PPU /A13 unconnected."
